num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Conceptual examples (not regulatory text)**\n\n- **Mutual fund (MF) class burdening ETF class:** MF cash purchases and redemptions force portfolio trading. Commissions, spreads and market impact fall on the whole portfolio, including ETF holders. Redemption-driven sales can also realize gains distributed to both classes.\n- **ETF class burdening MF class:** Cash creations, or custom baskets, can push trading costs or portfolio drift onto MF holders. Conversely, ETF in-kind redemptions shed low-basis lots, a tax benefit shared unevenly.\n\n**Monitoring categories**\n\n- **Transaction costs:** which class's flows cause trading, and whether fees or charges offset them.\n- **Cash:** liquidity buffers held for MF redemptions, which create cash drag for ETF holders.\n- **Gains:** capital-gain realizations and distributions attributable to each class's activity.\n\n**Representative order-specific framework (as of 2026-11-06)**\n\nUnder the share-class exemptive orders, the board approves policies to identify and address cross-subsidization and receives periodic adviser reporting. Metrics, frequency and escalation triggers are fund-specific under each order and compliance program. No universal thresholds apply.","ttft_ms":6264,"type":"result","duration_ms":10147,"uuid":"13307c94-30f7-4539-868d-d0cbff725363","ttft_stream_ms":1510,"time_to_request_ms":67,"first_content_frame_ms":1510,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
